            "popup_title": "Placebo-Controlled",
            "popup_text": "A \"placebo-controlled\" study is one in which one group receives the actual compound while another receives an inactive look-alike, or placebo. In this study, the placebo group received folic acid alone."
          }
        },
        "attr_blind": {
          "type": "attribute",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Double-blind",
            "popup_title": "Double-Blind",
            "popup_text": "\"Double-blind\" means neither participants nor researchers know who receives which product, preventing bias and ensuring objective results. This is the only blinded, placebo-controlled ovulation figure on this page — which is why it leads."
          }
        },
